#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:33
msgid "|morpheus| tracks memory at two levels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:35
msgid ""
"**Reserved memory** — Sum of all VM memory allocations on a host (what "
"VMs *could* use at maximum)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:36
msgid "**Used memory** — Actual memory consumption reported by the host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:38
msgid ""
"The capacity system uses ``computedMaxMemory`` (total − reserved system "
"overhead) as the denominator for utilization calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:41
msgid "Failover Capacity: N+1 Sizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:43
msgid ""
"N+1 sizing means that if any single host fails, the remaining hosts must "
"have enough available memory to absorb all VMs from the failed host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:46
msgid "Formula"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:48
msgid ""
"Required memory per host = Total VM memory / (N - 1)\n"
"Available per host must exceed = Largest single host's VM load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/capacity_planning.rst:53
msgid "Where N is the total number of hosts."
msgstr ""

